e": "Add files via upload\n\nThe PCA analysis reduced the multidimensional environmental dataset to two principal components (PC1 and PC2), which together explained approximately 75% of the total variance. This indicates that most of the underlying structure and patterns in the data\u2014such as variation in pollution, vegetation, and climate\u2014can be captured effectively in just two dimensions. The scatter plot reveals the distribution of observations in this reduced space, highlighting potential clusters or trends that may correspond to seasonal, geographic, or environmental differences. This dimensionality reduction provides a simplified yet meaningful view for further exploration and interpretation.", "created_at": "2025-06-06T19:07:40Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "083dba3c81e6fe9ab698f35fbd6ec67899babe6d", "message": "Create 2", "created_at": "2025-06-06T19:05:48Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4c4474094e467d681a7048b968fcd89d5d33f62a", "message": "Delete VARForecast/.md", "created_at": "2025-06-03T06:37:23Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7b6cf9ba4a495aa6547a3fd49fad7dfbb413dd01", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2025-06-03T06:36:59Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3da395508bca72afab3315926e9de093511eb33f", "message": "Create .md", "created_at": "2025-06-03T06:36:00Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "45dbfc722d233a9ef254db8d5883206d34f724d9", "message": "Delete Granger/Readme", "created_at": "2025-06-02T20:17:50Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1c86ec9e8a9cb0e608a8dd697808f84e32824524", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2025-06-02T20:17:23Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7b259788e5d0ca729df143e966f638c71fbc4488", "message": "Create Readme\n\n\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0627\u064b! \u062f\u0631 \u0627\u062f\u0627\u0645\u0647 \u06cc\u06a9 \u0645\u062a\u0646 \u0627\u0646\u06af\u0644\u06cc\u0633\u06cc \u0645\u0646\u0627\u0633\u0628 \u0628\u0631\u0627\u06cc \u067e\u0633\u062a LinkedIn \u062f\u0631\u0628\u0627\u0631\u0647 \u062a\u062d\u0644\u06cc\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u06cc\u062a \u06af\u0631\u0646\u062c\u0631 \u0648 \u06a9\u0627\u0631 \u0627\u0646\u062c\u0627\u0645\u200c\u0634\u062f\u0647 \u062f\u0631 \u0646\u0648\u062a\u200c\u0628\u0648\u06a9 \u0622\u0645\u0627\u062f\u0647 \u06a9\u0631\u062f\u0647\u200c\u0627\u0645. \u0627\u06cc\u0646 \u0645\u062a\u0646 \u062d\u0631\u0641\u0647\u200c\u0627\u06cc\u060c \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0635\u0631 \u0648 \u0642\u0627\u0628\u0644\u200c\u0641\u0647\u0645 \u0628\u0631\u0627\u06cc \u0645\u062e\u0627\u0637\u0628\u0627\u0646 \u062a\u062e\u0635\u0635\u06cc \u0648 \u0646\u06cc\u0645\u0647\u200c\u062a\u062e\u0635\u0635\u06cc \u0627\u0633\u062a:\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udcca Exploring Granger Causality in Environmental Time Series with Python \r\n\r\nUnderstanding causal relationships between variables is key in data-driven decision making\u2014especially in fields like environmental science and public health.\r\n\r\nThis week, I explored Granger Causality to analyze how variables like NDVI (vegetation index), temperature (LST), precipitation, evaporation, and particulate matter (PM) potentially influence each other over time.\r\n\r\nUsing Python and statistical tools, I:\r\n\u2705 Cleaned and structured time series data\r\n\u2705 Performed Granger causality tests on all variable combinations\r\n\u2705 Identified significant directional influences with p-values\r\n\u2705 Visualized the results in a heatmap and scatter plot using the Viridis colormap\r\n\r\nThe findings help highlight which variables might predict future changes in others, offering insights into environmental dynamics and potential interventions.\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udd17 If you're working with time series data, I highly recommend trying Granger causality\u2014it goes beyond correlation!\r\n\r\nCheck out the full Colab notebook here: (you can add the link to the notebook on GitHub or Google Drive)\r\n\r\n#DataScience #TimeSeries #Causality #Python #GrangerCausality #EnvironmentalData #MachineLearning #Analytics\r\n\r\n\u0627\u06af\u0631 \u0628\u062e\u0648\u0627\u06cc \u0627\u06cc\u0646 \u067e\u0633\u062a \u0631\u0648 \u0628\u0627 \u0644\u062d\u0646 \u063a\u06cc\u0631\u0631\u0633\u0645\u06cc\u200c\u062a\u0631\u060c \u0637\u0648\u0644\u0627\u0646\u06cc\u200c\u062a\u0631 \u06cc\u0627 \u0641\u0646\u06cc\u200c\u062a\u0631 \u0628\u0646\u0648\u06cc\u0633\u0645\u060c \u06cc\u0627 \u062a\u0631\u062c\u0645\u0647 \u0641\u0627\u0631\u0633\u06cc\u200c\u0634\u0648 \u0647\u0645 \u062f\u0627\u0634\u062a\u0647 \u0628\u0627\u0634\u06cc\u060c \u0628\u0627 \u06a9\u0645\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u06cc\u0644 \u0627\u0646\u062c\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u06cc\u200c\u062f\u0645.", "created_at": "2025-06-02T20:15:40Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "262c48d72c5c3affc9610adcd58f5e05f6cce911", "message": "Delete Granger", "created_at": "2025-06-02T20:13:56Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e7b862797b167457df36ec8494cff94005e67aed", "message": "Create Granger", "created_at": "2025-06-02T20:13:38Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "298400dfd415f6e37d37b283c46c0bf207c57333", "message": "Delete README directory", "created_at": "2025-06-02T20:13:10Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4d44c200f591b0f75e208cf254457741917332f3", "message": "Create GRANGER ANALYSIS \n\n\u062d\u062a\u0645\u0627\u064b! \u062f\u0631 \u0627\u062f\u0627\u0645\u0647 \u06cc\u06a9 \u0645\u062a\u0646 \u0627\u0646\u06af\u0644\u06cc\u0633\u06cc \u0645\u0646\u0627\u0633\u0628 \u0628\u0631\u0627\u06cc \u067e\u0633\u062a LinkedIn \u062f\u0631\u0628\u0627\u0631\u0647 \u062a\u062d\u0644\u06cc\u0644 \u0639\u0644\u06cc\u062a \u06af\u0631\u0646\u062c\u0631 \u0648 \u06a9\u0627\u0631 \u0627\u0646\u062c\u0627\u0645\u200c\u0634\u062f\u0647 \u062f\u0631 \u0646\u0648\u062a\u200c\u0628\u0648\u06a9 \u0622\u0645\u0627\u062f\u0647 \u06a9\u0631\u062f\u0647\u200c\u0627\u0645. \u0627\u06cc\u0646 \u0645\u062a\u0646 \u062d\u0631\u0641\u0647\u200c\u0627\u06cc\u060c \u0645\u062e\u062a\u0635\u0631 \u0648 \u0642\u0627\u0628\u0644\u200c\u0641\u0647\u0645 \u0628\u0631\u0627\u06cc \u0645\u062e\u0627\u0637\u0628\u0627\u0646 \u062a\u062e\u0635\u0635\u06cc \u0648 \u0646\u06cc\u0645\u0647\u200c\u062a\u062e\u0635\u0635\u06cc \u0627\u0633\u062a:\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udcca Exploring Granger Causality in Environmental Time Series with Python \r\n\r\nUnderstanding causal relationships between variables is key in data-driven decision making\u2014especially in fields like environmental science and public health.\r\n\r\nThis week, I explored Granger Causality to analyze how variables like NDVI (vegetation index), temperature (LST), precipitation, evaporation, and particulate matter (PM) potentially influence each other over time.\r\n\r\nUsing Python and statistical tools, I:\r\n\u2705 Cleaned and structured time series data\r\n\u2705 Performed Granger causality tests on all variable combinations\r\n\u2705 Identified significant directional influences with p-values\r\n\u2705 Visualized the results in a heatmap and scatter plot using the Viridis colormap\r\n\r\nThe findings help highlight which variables might predict future changes in others, offering insights into environmental dynamics and potential interventions.\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udd17 If you're working with time series data, I highly recommend trying Granger causality\u2014it goes beyond correlation!\r\n\r\nCheck out the full Colab notebook here: (you can add the link to the notebook on GitHub or Google Drive)\r\n\r\n#DataScience #TimeSeries #Causality #Python #GrangerCausality #EnvironmentalData #MachineLearning #Analytics\r\n\r\n\u0627\u06af\u0631 \u0628\u062e\u0648\u0627\u06cc \u0627\u06cc\u0646 \u067e\u0633\u062a \u0631\u0648 \u0628\u0627 \u0644\u062d\u0646 \u063a\u06cc\u0631\u0631\u0633\u0645\u06cc\u200c\u062a\u0631\u060c \u0637\u0648\u0644\u0627\u0646\u06cc\u200c\u062a\u0631 \u06cc\u0627 \u0641\u0646\u06cc\u200c\u062a\u0631 \u0628\u0646\u0648\u06cc\u0633\u0645\u060c \u06cc\u0627 \u062a\u0631\u062c\u0645\u0647 \u0641\u0627\u0631\u0633\u06cc\u200c\u0634\u0648 \u0647\u0645 \u062f\u0627\u0634\u062a\u0647 \u0628\u0627\u0634\u06cc\u060c \u0628\u0627 \u06a9\u0645\u0627\u0644 \u0645\u06cc\u0644 \u0627\u0646\u062c\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u06cc\u200c\u062f\u0645.", "created_at": "2025-06-02T20:11:19Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e99962c48e14c1e3cbc21a306d5800596cdc2c1a", "message": "Delete Corrolation power plant  directory", "created_at": "2025-06-02T16:46:13Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ff93bddb2bc6e6bb804cf314bfe260fad35cbe96", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2025-06-02T16:45:32Z", "repo": "Geemap-jupyter-notebook", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4a60d2478e83b653daf9e08a0a2c6f0adb7c53d8", "message": "Create README.md\n\n# \ud83d\udcca Descriptive and Correlation Analysis of Study Area\r\n\r\nThis project analyzes geographical and climate-related data from different provinces using descriptive statistics and correlation analysis.\r\n\r\n## \ud83e\uddfe